// A device written in Mojo (examples/mojo): its functions called from a
// `for` over a million entities on one thread and on many (Mojo's
// allocator and its caught errors on the program's threads), a buffer
// handed to it, and Mojo's print; the same either way, what C gives.
// Needs Mojo: examples/mojo/setup.sh, or `mojo` on the PATH.
// REQUIRES: mojo
// Its fns are read as they are built (mojodev.emit), and keep their word.
// RUN: %ent build --no-cache -I %S/../../examples/mojo %S/../../examples/mojo/calls.ent -o %t.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PURE --allow-empty
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/mojo %S/../../examples/mojo/calls.ent > %t.one
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/mojo %S/../../examples/mojo/calls.ent > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// PURE-NOT: warning
// CHECK: Mojo says hello, 42
// CHECK-NEXT: mixed 8790920353524676646 squares 9604000000 divided 174998885716 dot 37492162.5
